// _tests_/bit/testdecl/isolation.test.bit — CLI-level fixture for `test
// "name" { }` discovery (#4128, SPEC §19, epic #4126), driven through the
// built compiler by `_tests_/bit/clicmd/cases.bit`'s `testDeclCases`, the
// same way `_tests_/bit/testrunfilter/f.test.bit` drives the `--run`
// filter cases.
//
// RENAMED from `mixed.test.bit` by #4148 (the ticket removing the legacy
// shape-discovered test form). The old name and its content proved a `test
// "..." { }` declaration and a legacy bare `fn` were BOTH discovered from
// the same file — the decision that ticket owned. #4148 removed the legacy
// form outright (a bare, no-parameter, no-return `fn` in a `.test.bit` file
// is now E0117, a checker error — see
// `_tests_/bit/checkercases/check_bare_fn_test_shape.test.bit`), so there is
// no longer a second form to mix, and the old `legacyStillWorks` middle
// declaration is gone rather than reworded into something it no longer is.
//
// TWO properties remain, and are still worth their own fixture:
//
//   - ISOLATION (SPEC §19: "each test runs in its own process, so one
//     failure neither hides the others nor aborts the run"): "first test
//     panics" is declared FIRST — the load-bearing position, matching
//     testgencheck.bit's own convention — and its sibling must still run
//     and report after it.
//   - `--run` MATCHES THE DISPLAY STRING, not a symbol: "second test also
//     passes" contains a space, which no Bit identifier can, so a run
//     filtered by a pattern containing one can only match by reading the
//     STRING the author wrote (testgen.bit's `TestDiscovery.names`), never
//     the internal `test$<n>` call symbol a `test` declaration actually
//     lowers to.

test "first test panics" {
  assert(false)
}

test "second test also passes" {
  assert(2 * 3 == 6)
}
